From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 19:41:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: check the index cache allocations in
 fetchListHTTP()

Neither allocation made for a new http_index_cache entry is checked.

malloc() is dereferenced on the next line by fetchInitURLList(), so a
failure there faults immediately.  fetchCopyURL() is worse: it returns
NULL on failure, the entry keeps a NULL location, and if the listing
then succeeds the entry is linked into index_cache -- where the lookup
loop of the next call dereferences it as cache->location->scheme.

fetchCopyURL() already reports the error itself, so only the malloc
needs a fetch_syserr().

Signed-off-by: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
---
 libfetch/http.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfetch/http.c b/libfetch/http.c
index 060ced3..2bbfa0e 100644
--- a/libfetch/http.c
+++ b/libfetch/http.c
@@ -1492,8 +1492,16 @@ fetchListHTTP(struct url_list *ue, struct url *url, const char *pattern, const c
 		}
 
 		cache = malloc(sizeof(*cache));
+		if (cache == NULL) {
+			fetch_syserr();
+			return -1;
+		}
 		fetchInitURLList(&cache->ue);
 		cache->location = fetchCopyURL(url);
+		if (cache->location == NULL) {
+			free(cache);
+			return -1;
+		}
 	}
 
 	f = fetchGetHTTP(url, flags);
